(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #156: an element of a list parameter, named in a local
 and then appended, keeps its own type, whatever the top-level list that
 shares the parameter's name holds.)

To 'copy each kind' with a list called shelf and a list called placed.
    a text called word is element 1 of shelf.
    append word to placed.
    a map called section is element 2 of shelf.
    append section to placed.
    a list called pair is element 3 of shelf.
    append pair to placed.
    a float called weight is element 4 of shelf.
    append weight to placed.
    a boolean called ready is element 5 of shelf.
    append ready to placed.

To 'copy a name' with a list called names and a list called placed.
    a text called name is element 1 of names.
    append name to placed.

To 'copy a section' with a list called sections and a list called placed.
    a map called section is element 1 of sections.
    append section to placed.

a list called names is ["alpha"].
a list called sections is [{"name": ".text", "size": 10}].
a list called shelf is ["beta", {"size": 4}, [1, 2], 2.5, true].
a list called placed is [].
'copy a name' with names and placed.
'copy a section' with sections and placed.
'copy each kind' with shelf and placed.
Print "{placed}".
For each item in placed, print item's type.

To 'copy a later name' with a list called words and a list called kept.
    a text called word is element 1 of words.
    append word to kept.
    a list called pair is element 2 of words.
    append pair to kept.

a list called words is ["gamma", [3]].
a list called kept is [].
'copy a later name' with words and kept.
Print "{kept}".

a map called stock is element 2 of shelf.
a list called held is element 3 of shelf.
a text called label is element 1 of shelf.
a list called gathered is [].
append stock to gathered.
append held to gathered.
append label to gathered.
Print "{gathered}".
For each item in gathered, print item's type.
